---
# OIDC login to the API server with the Pocket ID (docs/cluster/README.md#oidc-authentication).
# Control plane only: every node of this cluster is one.
# `talosctl validate` checks the keys of this document, not the content of `configuration`:
# machined checks its types, the API server all of it at its start. A change restarts the API
# server of the node (its static pod), which does not start with an invalid config: apply one
# node at a time, and check it (`kubectl auth whoami` through it) before the other. A valid but
# wrong value (a misspelled claim) starts: the login shows it.
# A patch replaces the whole `configuration` of Talos: its default `anonymous` is repeated below.
# No `apiVersion` nor `kind`: machined sets them in the file (`apiserver.config.k8s.io/v1beta1`).
apiVersion: v1alpha1
kind: KubeAuthenticationConfig
configuration:
  # The default of Talos 1.14: the health endpoints without credentials, for the probes of the
  # static pod and `just bootstrap api-ready`. The API server refuses a reload that changes it.
  anonymous:
    enabled: true
    conditions:
      - path: /livez
      - path: /readyz
      - path: /healthz
  jwt:
    - issuer:
        url: {{ oidc.issuer }}
        # One client per tool that sends its ID token to the API server (not the Flux UI: it
        # checks its token itself and impersonates the user). MatchAny: a token is accepted when
        # its `aud` holds one of them.
        audiences:
          - {{ oidc.kubelogin_client_id }}
          - {{ oidc.headlamp_client_id }}
        audienceMatchPolicy: MatchAny
      claimMappings:
        # Set by the admins of the Pocket ID, the users cannot change it. Prefixed, as the
        # groups, so that it cannot match a user or a group of Kubernetes (`system:`).
        username:
          claim: preferred_username
          prefix: "oidc:"
        groups:
          claim: groups
          prefix: "oidc:"
        # Stable when the username changes: the id of the user in the audit log.
        uid:
          claim: sub
